<title>FRANCE: EU grain group confirms tax rises, bids rejected.</title>
<headline>EU grain group confirms tax rises, bids rejected.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission has rejected all bids for wheat export licences pesented since August 1, grain trade group Coceral confirmed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It also confirmed increases in export taxes on soft wheat, durum wheat and a variety of related products.</p>
<p>Brussels-based Coceral, which liaises with the EU for the grain trade, said all bids for licences between August 1 and August 4 had been rejected.</p>
<p>No volume was given but officials had reported bids for at least 832,500 tonnes of soft wheat at a tax of 0.5 Ecus per tonne. Those bids were made through France on Friday and Monday.  </p>
<p>Coceral gave the following breakdown in Ecus per tonne.</p>
<p>				   New tax	    Previous tax</p>
<p> CATEGORY		     (August 5)	   (July 31)</p>
<p> Durum wheat grain	    10.00		    5.00</p>
<p> Soft wheat grain		3.00		    0.50</p>
<p> Durum wheat flour	    15.00		    7.50</p>
<p> Soft wheat flour		4.00		    0.70</p>
<p> Durum semolina		 15.00		    7.50</p>
<p> Soft wheat semolina	   4.00		    0.70</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
